From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:40:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sio: Expose the S5L8960X MCA1 transmit endpoint

The iPad mini 2 (J85) plays its speakers through MCA1 of its A7, whose
transmit endpoint is SmartIO 0x2a in its ADT (/arm-io/mca1
dma-channels, iOS 12.5.8 16H88). Add it next to MCA0's 0x28/0x29. The
firmware and the shared DMA implementation are unchanged; the shim words
come from the MCA, per channel.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c
index 2aa667208..0fc5b5928 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c
@@ -1224,9 +1224,13 @@ static const struct apple_sio_hw apple_sio_t7000_hw = {
 	.num_dma_ranges = ARRAY_SIZE(apple_sio_t7000_dma_ranges),
 };
 
-/* MCA0, the codec's link, as described by the J72 ADT */
+/*
+ * MCA0, the codec's link, as described by the J72 ADT, and MCA1 TX, the
+ * iPad mini 2's (J85) speaker link, as its ADT describes it
+ */
 static const struct apple_sio_dma_range apple_sio_s5l8960x_dma_ranges[] = {
 	{ 0x28, 0x29 },
+	{ 0x2a, 0x2a },
 };
 
 /*
